# AI Code Review & Evaluation Lab

A portfolio project for evaluating AI-generated code with a repeatable, evidence-based review process.

The lab documents correctness, bug severity, edge cases, test evidence, complexity, and corrected implementations across Python, C++, and JavaScript. It also includes a small Python CLI for validating evaluation records and calculating a transparent rubric score.

> **Scope note:** The sample evaluations in this repository are illustrative, authored examples—not results from a real model benchmark. Replace or extend them with evaluations you personally perform, and record the model, prompt, date, and environment when you evaluate real outputs.

## Goals

- Review generated code for correctness and maintainability.
- Identify bugs and classify their severity consistently.
- Design edge-case tests instead of relying only on happy paths.
- Explain time and space complexity.
- Compare solutions using documented evidence rather than intuition.
- Maintain reproducible, readable evaluation records.

